tags: []
date: 2026-03-09T00:00:00-04:00
---

Sir Arctos is a polar bear who gained speech and reason, a knight of the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]]. He was brought from [[Geography/Austrene/index|Austrene]] and knighted by Aurelia VII, the Church's pontifex. He wears pearlescent plate over his fur, a purple cloak and a wide-brimmed hat, and carries a bastard sword and a shield. He keeps a monocle for poor sight in one eye, and calls himself a very smart bear. He eats from a bowl stamped with his name, using silver cutlery.

Anzu, meeting him, knew of no tribe of speaking polar bears and took him for either a druid who preferred the shape of a bear or an animal awakened by divine energy. He joined [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]] in the wake of the deaths at the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|Crowded Flea]].

In the white void above Save Your Soul Incorporated he asked [[Aut]] for one of his marks and took it on his chest. It hides by default and can be shown at will, will not appear to anyone who has already seen his bare skin without it, and shows on its own to anyone who has seen his skin with it. Aut offered to remove it, and does not compel his friends into his service.

Before the assault on the Gas-n-Go he had his sword silvered, and in the fane beneath it he dispelled the black cape that fought at Tywelwyn's shoulder.

Below the throne he went on into the deeper fane, and the [[Gas-n-Go Heart|Heart]] there named him one of the Poncho Boys. In the armory he took the white armband from its case, and [[People/Argyle|Argyle]]'s fortress shield, grappling gun and gold. When the gang's shift crew came at ten that night, the werebear among them swelled to fill the hall and pinned him against a wall.

After the fane he went with the others to the [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Inquisition/index|Inquisition]]'s office and asked for the two Inquisitors [[Aut]] had named, Penitence and Absolution. In the questioning room below the lobby he told the story straight, and asked Inquisitor [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Inquisition/People/Inquisitor Penitence|Penitence]] about joining the order; Penitence told him no ritual could be worked on an adult bear. He asked Penitence to carry word of their report to his friend Vane, and was refused.

He was bitten and seized by the [[Bestiary/Lovelorn|lovelorn]] in [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Detective Ellis Brooks|Brooks]]'s flat, and one latched onto his face and would not let go until he knocked it off. He healed the others up afterwards. He casts [[Phenomena/Augury|augury]], and asked whether the Party should try to rescue Brooks; the answer came back as the four of them as zombies, and they let him go. That night he prayed to the [[Iridescent Host|Host]] and asked why he had been awakened when he could have stayed a sleeping bear, and got no answer.

At the parking-lot sale he tried to sell the buyers the Aventine as well and was refused, and he took the Crystal Globe card they left. Back at the bar he paid Smiler to register the Aventine under his name and bought healer's gloves. At the cabin at void 26 he helped unbolt the bed Anaïs was chained to, and the shackle opened at a thought for him, as it did for Benny and Johnny, while Anzu could not open it. He asked Anaïs why Renge and Aut were at odds and whether the Pontifex served Renge, and for it Anaïs called him the most fair-weather bear he had met.

Before the midnight sale he visited a small [[Iridescent Host|Host]] church near the [[Sin and Tonic]] to network. It was not ornate, kept only a single prayer engine, and was run by one low-ranking priest, the sort of man he judged good enough for a dock worker. Arctos asked about starting a parish of his own and was told he would need to speak with the pre-existing convocs in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]]; [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Illmari Vaino|Illmari]] would not have a prayer group in his bar.

The two days before the pilgrimage he spent at the small [[Iridescent Host|Host]] church near the [[Sin and Tonic]], making himself a known quantity there and working toward becoming a guest preacher. Since he is known by his pearlescent plate, he got a plain half plate from [[Org/The Undertable/People/Smiler|Smiler]] to wear in its place. [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anouk Marchal|Anouk]] had broken the arcane lock on the journal taken from [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]], and he leafed through it: three months of daily entries, Hlarf's own diary, recording coins skimmed from the Roundhat rackets and some competent if slanting poetry. One entry from two months before mentioned driving through the ring into [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]] to meet someone, and no name, because Hlarf knew who it was.

The Party dyed him black and put a collar on him so he could pass as a pet black bear at the gathering, though he was far too big for one. At the rest-stop gas station on the way the Party was ambushed by robbers, and afterward he healed the others on the drive. In [[Geography/Calaria/Ragged Roost|Ragged Roost]] the town flattened every raiment to the same gray, but when he pulled up his breastplate and called the three dots of [[Aut]]'s mark, they showed and still answered him.

At the pilgrimage he wore a plain half plate and the black dye, and was handed a dragon mask, one of the plain white ones that press to any face. He waited in the fortune teller's line with [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] and talked with the guests around him until Johnny sent word that the other path led to gladiator combat, and then he left the line to join it. He offered salmon jerky to a man ahead of him and asked him about [[Geography/Raelion/index|Raelion]], and the man took him for a poisoner and told him not to talk to him, and the man behind told him that asking after the gods defeated the point of the raiment. [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] said the remark had knocked the wind out of him.

In the train yard the wheel landed on red, and he warded [[People/Benny|Benny]] with fireproofing and took his place on the floor against three [[Bestiary/Barbazu|Barbazu]] and a [[Bestiary/Brimorak|Brimorak]]. He cast a crisis of faith on one devil and was cut for it, and the wound would not stop bleeding. When [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] and [[People/Benny|Benny]] went down and [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] lay unconscious, he cast a heal over the fallen, and an aurora broke from him as it took hold and woke them; the others knew then that the [[Iridescent Host|Host]] had saved them. Afterward he worked over Anzu and Benny to stop their bleeding, and then over himself.

At the pilgrimage he sat out the association game on the fairy-ring path, allowed to aid the others but not to step into the rings, and worked the riddle of the prism potions with [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] until Anzu reached in and pulled out the key. At the Vane manor in the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Aurideon/index|Aurideon]] he was Master Arctos to the guards and the majordomo, and waited in his old rooms for the minister to come back from the council.

At the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Masque District/Belvedere Library|Belvedere library]] he helped [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] sort through the periodicals. He learned he has a fan club of five in [[Geography/Calaria/index|Calaria]], now all in prison for trying to break into Vane's manor to meet him; an interview they gave while being arrested said they knew it was not his fault, and he meant to call on them at some point.

At the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus|Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus]] he pulled a hooded poncho up over his plate so as not to stand out, and offered to find the Heart a respectable painting; the Heart's servant told them that if they could get one, they would have brought it. Outside, [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] named the museum as the place to learn what a good painting was.

At the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Metropolitan Conservatory|MetCon]] he took a free tour and asked the guide so many questions that she had to buffer her answers, drawing out the whole list of works on show and the story of the museum's one heist. He offered the children his autograph, and when the guide heard he wanted bear art she sent him down the road to a Museum of Supernatural History. At [[People/Valerius Vane|Vane]]'s manor he asked [[People/Crowley Hart|Crowley]] for the [[People/Kellum Quinn|Kellum Quinn]] painting in the parlor and was allowed to take it, and he collected two paintings of his own from his rooms; all three went into the armory at [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]]. He told Crowley he thought Grayson was behind whatever had the council in a stir, and that the Inquisitors were investigating him. At 414 Anchor Street he was invisible when the fight began, dispelled the darkness Sbrtlby called down, and shook the demon's bones until it died.

He asked the twins to build a radio tuned to a frequency he gave them. At the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus|Sub Transit Nexus]] he threw the Quinn into [[Org/Prime Meridian/Rapid Connection|Rapid Connection]]'s central cortex and opened the golden box the Heart gave back, and asked the Heart what else it liked besides paintings. He offered [[People/Hogan Voss Darkmoor|the Archmechanic]] chocolates, coffee and a seat at a sports game, and was told the man lives on IV packs and cannot leave the building for long. In the lobby he was left deaf by one of [[Org/Concordia/People/Louis Maller|Louis Maller]]'s blasts.

After the Concordia fight he wrote the two agents into the little notebook he keeps in the back of the car, crossed them out with the demon already crossed out, and left [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anouk Marchal|Anouk]]'s name with a question mark; the Party kept the question mark.

Over downtime he began the paperwork for a licence to grow and sell [[Phenomena/Shiver|shiver]]. The [[People/Valerius Vane|Vane]] name is too entrenched to be hurt by it, and a distant cousin in the Grayson family, most of whom are in medicine, could be paid a kickback from the Vane estate to grant the licence for a medicinal grow. He has the classiest room at the [[Sin and Tonic]], with two paintings, a bed the size of a giant dog bed, a chest freezer of food from home, and a whiskey glass holding nothing but ice.
